In article <1990Feb21.013402.28142@max.sunysb.edu> rosalia@max.sunysb.edu (Mark Galassi) writes:
+
+  Many people have seen rich sectors, and later these sectors
+  have lost all their gold mine points.  Sometimes even WITH NO
+  UPDATE!

Guess what:

    "It's not a bug, it's a feature!"

A nation is able to see a sector containing jewels, based on the type
of materials in the sector, and the wealth of the nation.

If the wealth of a nation drops, the ability to see such sectors
drops.  Things that can affect wealth include: lose of jewels through
magic purchase, lose of money due to conversion to jewels.

In one of my patches, I lessened the affect of one turn transitions,
such as magic purchases can have... I do not remember which patch did
this, it might have been patch 7.  Also, the next version of conquer
will chance the wealth calculation to be based on production not
storage, so it will be much more accurate.

